<DocsLayout
  title="huberclaude on OpenRouter — one key, every model"
  description="huberclaude runs only on OpenRouter. Sign in with /login, pick any model from the OpenRouter catalog with /model, and track your balance with /usage."
  heading="openrouter"
  lede="huberclaude is dedicated to OpenRouter. One API key gets you the whole catalog, and you skip provider setup entirely."
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="why-openrouter-only">why openrouter only</h2>
  <p>
    huberclaude is a fork of <a href="https://github.com/Gitlawb/openclaude" rel="noopener">openclaude</a>
    with multi-provider support removed. Every request goes to
    <code>https://openrouter.ai/api/v1</code>. Any inherited <code>OPENAI_BASE_URL</code>
    or model, such as one exported for a local proxy, is overridden, so a stray export
    can't send your code somewhere else. Because there is one transport, there's one
    behavior to learn.
  </p>
  <p>
    To spend fewer tokens, pair OpenRouter with <a href="/docs/enxame/">enxame mode</a>,
    which offloads mechanical sub-tasks to a swarm of cheap z.ai workers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="login">sign in with /login</h2>
  <p>
    Start <code>huberclaude</code> and run <code>/login</code>. Paste your key from
    <a href="https://openrouter.ai/keys" rel="noopener">openrouter.ai/keys</a>. You can
    also set a custom base URL there. The key is saved to
    <code>~/.openclaude/config.json</code> with owner-only (<code>0600</code>) permissions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="models">pick a model</h2>
  <p>
    Run <code>/model</code> to browse the OpenRouter catalog and switch models
    mid-session. The default is <code>qwen/qwen3-coder</code>. Pick models with strong
    tool and function calling for the best agent results.
  </p>

  <h2 id="usage">track spend with /usage</h2>
  <p>
    <code>/usage</code> shows your OpenRouter balance and spend as a fuel gauge
    scaled to your last recharge.
  </p>

  <h2 id="env-setup">env-var setup</h2>
  <p>For CI and scripted <code>--print</code> runs, export the key instead of using <code>/login</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>export HUBERCLAUDE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
huberclaude -p "explain this repo"</code></pre>
  <p>
    A key saved with <code>/login</code> takes precedence. The generic
    <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code> is ignored on purpose, so an unrelated export can't
    switch the account your session uses. See the
    <a href="/docs/configuration/#environment-variables">configuration page</a> for the
    other variables.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
